<title>MOLDOVA: MOLDOVAN SPECIALISED INSURANCE BOND YIELD EDGES UP.</title>
<headline>MOLDOVAN SPECIALISED INSURANCE BOND YIELD EDGES UP.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield on Moldovan 365-day</p>
<p>specialised insurance bonds edged up on Tuesday to 34.38</p>
<p>percent annual from 34.35 percent at the previous auction on</p>
<p>February 25, a National Bank official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Full details of the 365-day insurance bonds auction:</p>
<p>				March 18	 Feb 25</p>
<p> Issue volume		2.00 mln lei  3.00 mln lei</p>
<p> Denominations	     1,000 lei     1,000 lei</p>
<p> Nominal demand	   17.85 mln	31.79 mln</p>
<p> Volume sold		0.7 mln	  2.7 mln</p>
<p> Yield			34.38 pct	34.35 pct</p>
<p> Price			86.0 pct	 85.6 pct</p>
<p> Range of bids	    86.0-88.4 pct  85.6-92.0 pct</p>
<p> Maturity		   March 20, 1997 Feb 27, 1998</p>
<p>NOTE - The yield includes a fixed annual income of 15</p>
<p>percent guaranteed by the Finance Ministry.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
